      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Without the unwavering conviction of a towering figure such as Robespierre, the Revolution would have been nothing more than a predictable, self-devouring frenzy of the common mob.\n\n He was the necessary, strong hand that could take the inchoate anger of the people and channel it toward a coherent, revolutionary *end*, a political objective beyond the next good strong bread.\n\n He is the very structure that could have saved the ideological core of the change from being utterly devoured by pure, aimless violence and the self-interest of the unguided crowd.\n\n \"",
      "source": "target",
